          "kicker": "Contract extension",
          "heading": "Sean Jansen commits to Connacht as Ireland back-rower signs extension",
          "body": "Ireland number eight Sean Jansen has signed a two-year contract extension, keeping him with Connacht until at least 2029. The 27-year-old, who made his international debut against Japan this summer, enjoyed a standout campaign last season, scoring 12 tries in 20 appearances. Connacht head coach Stuart Lancaster described the deal as a “massive boost” for the province, citing Jansen’s recent form and commitment as a major statement of intent ahead of the new United Rugby Championship season."
