          "heading": "Professional players express ongoing frustration regarding smaller ball trial adoption plans",
          "body": "The trial of the smaller ball in the WXV Global Series continues to draw scrutiny from international players. While World Rugby has moved to expand the testing period, concerns regarding the performance impact persist. Players have been vocal about the transition, with England fly-half Zoe Harrison describing the change as the worst decision ever. With the trial period set to conclude in October, stakeholders remain divided on whether this adjustment is a viable long-term solution for the women’s game."
